  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v4.9.4-rc.2: completes the configurable Wasm linear-memory ceiling. rc.1 made the host-side `WebAssembly.Memory` `maximum` configurable via `WasmBackendOptions.MaxLinearMemoryPages` but the compiled kernel module's WASM binary still hardcoded `maximum=16384` in its memory-import declaration; consumers that raised the host cap above 16384 hit `WebAssembly.instantiate(): memory import has a larger maximum size N than the module's declared maximum 16384` on every kernel dispatch (Data found this on DA3 with `MaxLinearMemoryPages=32768`). rc.2 threads the same value through `WasmBackend.CreateKernel` -> `WasmModuleBuilder.ImportSharedMemory` so both ends agree. Default behavior unchanged (consumers using the 16384 default see identical bytes). Required by `SpawnDev.ILGPU.ML`'s DA3-Small graph executor. Note: the cached memory's maximum is fixed at instantiation; raising the option after the accelerator already reused the cached memory has no effect. See [CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md) for the full per-version history.",
